  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WASH response to tropical storm Ana in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">18000</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to mitigate the effects of Tropical Storm Ana in selected wards in Zimbabwe by distributing 2000 hygiene kits to targeted households and rehabilitating of 2 piped water supply systems that were destroyed by the cyclone. Hygiene education campaigns will target 18000 people and water treatment chemicals will be distributed to 4839 households to prevent diarrheal&#xA0;outbreaks. Food aid to 100 most vulnerable households will be distributed. Capacity of local Disaster Risk Reduction structures (ward level) will be strengthened.</narrative>
  </description>
